    "The optional four-cell microbenchmark uses synthetic checkpoint-like and same-bank-stress fixtures; it is a kernel promotion gate, not a model or serving-throughput result.",
    "CUDA compute-sanitizer device memcheck did not run because GPU debugging features are disabled on this Orin; the two exit-99 logs must not be interpreted as device-memory-check passes.",
    "ASan and UBSan instrument host C++ only; they do not instrument the CUDA device code.",
    "The production promotion is limited to exact aligned M18 NVFP4 [17408,5120] and [5120,17408] projections; other shapes and alignments retain ordered fallbacks.",
    "M18 gate and up remain serial on one stream. The inherited auxiliary-stream route applies only to exact C32 gate/up, and this milestone adds no double/triple buffering, phase overlap, or Prefill/Decode overlap.",
    "The end-to-end benchmark is batch-one generation for one tokenizer-pinned short prompt and one output token; it excludes engine-load time and does not establish concurrent-request or serving throughput.",
    "The Nsight comparison uses separate baseline and candidate processes and is consistent with, but does not replace, the unprofiled B-C-C-B timing gate.",
    "Raw logs, binaries, and profiler reports are local evidence and are not checked into the repository."
